 light on that truth imusama  decides to extinguish that light from  history as the victor of the ancient war  imusama writes history in the way that  he or she sees fit just like the Romans  wrote the history of the Punic Wars in a  way that made them look Noble and  civilized while making the carthaginians  appear to be cruel and barbaric some  historians believe that the Romans  invented stories about Carthage doing  horrible things like human sacrifices  just to make themselves look better by  comparison however whether or not the  carthaginians really engaged in such  practices remains a matter of debate  among historians again there is very  little that we actually know about them  which is exactly what the Romans  intended but even if yumusama is the  immortal ruler of the world government  in the present time what role did this  person play during the void century was  he or she someone who actually fought  against Joy boy meaning that emu must  also have absolutely incredible Powers  after all the original joyboy had the  overpowered Nika fruit so could emu also  have a Godly Zone devil fruit or maybe  some other absolutely broken power or  could it be that emu actually fought  alongside Joy boy but then betrayed him  in exchange for power and immortality  this is just my personal hunch by the  way but I've always had the feeling that  imusama would turn out to be a woman emu  just strikes me as an evil queen type  character kind of like Maleficent from  Sleeping Beauty if that does turn out to  be the case I wonder if there will be  some sort of forbidden love or  unrequited love element to her  relationship with the original Joy boy  whatever the connection is I do think  that there will be an important link  between joyboy and emu and that link  will play a major role in the final arcs  of the story as Luffy the New Joy boy  takes on the world government once and  for all I am convinced that the events  of the Void Century will closely  parallel the Puni